hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18108","Abdul-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Majma ibn Yaqoub, from the people of Quba, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to me that some of his family said to his grandfather on his mother's side, who was Abdullah ibn Abi Habibah: What did you witness of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: He came to us in this mosque of ours, so I came and sat beside him, then drink was brought, so he drank, then he passed it to me while I was on his right. He said: And I saw him that day pray in his sandals, while I was then a boy."
